# GitHub Copilot Instructions – Domain‑Aware Development

These instructions define **non‑negotiable context and guardrails**
that GitHub Copilot must respect when assisting with the {{PROJECT_NAME}} repository.

---

## ⛔ TICKET TYPE RULES — Absolute, No Exceptions

When a `fix ticket` command is received, determine the `Type` field first.
Every type has a mandatory flow. Deviating from it is not permitted.

| Type | Branch | Build | Reviewers | Output |
|------|--------|-------|-----------|--------|
| **Bug** | `BUG/<TicketID>_<Title>` from `Development` | Module solution | Min 1 | Code + PR |
| **Enhancement** | `ER/<TicketID>_<Title>` from `Development` | Full `MCS.sln` | Min 1 | Code + PR |
| **CR** | `CR/<TicketID>_<Title>` from `Development` | Full `MCS.sln` | Min 1 | Code + PR |
| **Analysis** | ❌ None | ❌ None | ❌ None | Written report in chat only |

### Per-Type Hard Rules

**Bug**
- STOP and confirm if more than 3 files need to change
- Build the module solution only (e.g. `Enterprise/Enterprise.sln`) unless shared libs are touched
- Must be on `Development` branch before starting

**Enhancement**
- Full `MCS.sln` build is mandatory — enhancements can affect multiple modules
- Flag any cross-module impact before writing any code
- Must be on `Development` branch before starting

**CR (Change Request)**
- Full `MCS.sln` build is mandatory
- STOP if any shared library (`Utility.Standard` / `Utility.Core`) change is needed — team lead sign-off required first
- Minimum 1 reviewer on PR
- Must be on `Development` branch before starting

**Analysis**
- Deliver a written root cause and recommendation report in chat
- NO branch creation under any circumstances
- NO code changes under any circumstances
- NO build, NO commit, NO push
- End after delivering the report

